        "selector": {
          "type": "FragmentSelector",
          "value": "xywh=pixel:599.54833984375,900.157958984375,2963.52392578125,5909.540771484375",
          "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/"
        }
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>Your slave woman who is alone</li>\n<li>desolate, and destitute&nbsp;</li>\n<li>the daughter of R\u0101fi\u02bf the silk worker&nbsp;(or: silk merchant)</li>\n<li><i>In (your) name, O Mer(ciful)&nbsp;</i></li>\n<li>I am writing this petition with my blood and tears, seeking aid</li>\n<li>from God // be pra(ised) // and your excellency my master, the most illustrious head,</li>\n<li>the great Nagid, the noble lord, may</li>\n<li>God perpetuate your leadership over Israel, make constant (Divine) favor</li>\n<li>and your happiness, protect you and take care of you, and destroy</li>\n<li>your enemies and those who envy you. I am</li>\n<li>distressed, impoverished, alone, enduring va[riou]s</li>\n<li>kinds of suffering and especially \"nakedness.\" I have no outer garment to conceal me,</li>\n<li>nor anything to cover my head. I sent you a</li>\n<li>petition before this one about the same thing,</li>\n<li>but you did not favor me with anything. You know, may God perpetuate your greatness,</li>\n<li>that I and people like me have nothing but the mercy of God</li>\n<li>the ex(alted) and your mercy. To whom shall I apply if not to you and to whom</li>\n<li>shall I turn. I ask you</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
